    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 91 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5755\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 91 of the laws of 2008, amending the public health law,\nrelating to establishing a task force on toll plaza air quality, in\nrelation to the expiration thereof\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis legislation will extend the provisions of chapter\n91/2008 which established a task force to study the air quality in\ntoll plazas.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would extend for one year the task\nforce on air quality in toll plazas in New York City.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nAir pollution can affect an individual's health in many\nways with both short-term and long-term effects. The extent to which\nan individual is harmed by air pollution usually depends on the total\nexposure to the damaging chemicals. In many cases, employees working\nin toll plazas are exposed to these harmful pollutants for a total of\n8 hours per day. The task force on toll plaza air quality is\nrequired-in order to identify, study and determine the extent of the\neffects on air quality in toll plazas leading into and out of the\nfive boroughs of New York city.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nChapter 91/2008 established the task force on air quality in toll\nplazas and required a report from the task force. The report has not\nbeen produced. This bill would extend the task force in order to\nproduce the report.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall be effective immediately and shall be\ndeemed to have been in full force and effect on April 1, 2011 when\nchapter 91/2008 expired.\n\n",
